commit 94c554da6fb5001ce09d213c26987d22833d6b5c
Author: Pavlo Vynychenko <<redacted-email>>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 00:57:58 2026 +0200

    DLSS: set the screen percentage at the priority it was last set by

    T-102 sets the render scale through the user settings, which sets
    r.ScreenPercentage above the scalability priority that DLSS used, so a DLSS mode
    could be ignored and the scene rendered at 100%. The percentage is now set at its
    last setter's priority, and the log line shows the value the engine holds.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <<redacted-email>>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dd7nAQrerLmhufyK6ycPjz

